    "parameter_source": "engineering_assumption",
    "vendor_confirmed": false,
    "notes": "Textbook-order fiber lengths and pumps. Peak cross sections at 1530 nm (sigma_a=6.72e-25, sigma_e=6.55e-25 m^2) and lifetime 10 ms follow the iXblue EDF datasheet; the spectral shape is a Gaussian fit, not measured. erbium_area_m2 is an assumption (10 um^2). Not a vendor specification. The GFF loss_spectrum_db is an invented notch (28 dB at 1530 nm) that suppresses the 1530 nm ASE peak; it is not a vendor curve. Fiber lengths (8/5/10 m) and pump powers (100/250/800 mW) were chosen by a parameter sweep so that the 8-channel demo gives about 18 dBm total output; they are not vendor values. Channels: 8 on a 100 GHz grid from 193.1 THz (1546.9-1552.5 nm, near the centre of the C band); the real plan must come from the vendor."
